Keep a user-config default silently when the setting is simply absent.

STK logs an [error] for every setting config.xml does not name:

  User Config: Unknown value for fullscreen; expected true or false
  User Config: Couldn't find parameter group ipv4-stun-servers

The stk launcher seeds a minimal config.xml (enable_internet plus two
attributes of <Video>), so every boot printed ~20 of these -- 12 500 across
the UART archive -- and a genuinely malformed value would drown among them.
An absent setting is the normal state of a fresh or older config: the default
stands and STK writes the full file back on exit.

- BoolUserConfigParam::findYourDataInAnAttributeOf / findYourDataInAChildOf:
  return quietly when XMLNode::get() finds no attribute (it returns 0); a value
  that is present and neither "true" nor "false" is still reported.
- MapUserConfigParam::findYourDataInAChildOf: an absent group returns
  quietly, as GroupUserConfigParam::findYourDataInAChildOf already does
  (upstream commented its message out). "Invalid name" / "Invalid key name"
  for a malformed entry stay.

--- a/src/config/user_config.cpp
+++ b/src/config/user_config.cpp
@@ -252,8 +252,10 @@
     const XMLNode* child = node->getNode(m_param_name);
     if (child == NULL)
     {
-        Log::error("User Config", "Couldn't find parameter group %s",
-          m_param_name.c_str());
+        // PHOENIX: an absent group is not an error -- keep the default
+        // silently, as GroupUserConfigParam does (upstream commented its
+        // message out). A config.xml that names only a few settings, like the
+        // one the stk launcher seeds, otherwise logs every group it omits.
         return;
     }
     for (unsigned i = 0; i < child->getNumNodes(); i++)
@@ -539,7 +541,9 @@
     if(child == NULL) return;
 
     std::string text_value = "";
-    child->get( "value", &text_value );
+    // PHOENIX: no value attribute = keep the default silently; only a value
+    // that is present and neither "true" nor "false" is reported.
+    if (!child->get( "value", &text_value )) return;
 
     if(text_value == "true")
     {
@@ -559,7 +563,10 @@
 void BoolUserConfigParam::findYourDataInAnAttributeOf(const XMLNode* node)
 {
     std::string text_value = "";
-    node->get( m_param_name, &text_value );
+    // PHOENIX: an absent attribute = keep the default silently (a group
+    // element that names only some of its members, e.g. the launcher's
+    // <Video show_fps=... />); a present, malformed value is still reported.
+    if (!node->get( m_param_name, &text_value )) return;
 
     if (text_value == "true")
     {
